---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 10, 2026';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that govern your use of MobileFlow."
  eyebrow="Legal"
>
  <p>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

  <p>
    These terms govern your use of MobileFlow, a service built and operated by HexaOne Labs. By
    creating an account, you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    MobileFlow connects to a GitHub repository you authorize, triggers builds through GitHub Actions
    on your behalf, and returns signed Android and iOS binaries. Builds run on GitHub-hosted runners
    and consume your own GitHub Actions minutes.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You're responsible for the repositories you connect and the secrets you upload. Only authorize
    access to repositories you have the right to build, and revoke MobileFlow's GitHub access at any
    time from your dashboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Early access &amp; refund guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    MobileFlow is still under active development. Early access purchased for CHF 250 grants lifetime
    access once the product is available. If we have not granted you product access by <strong
      >December 31, 2026</strong
    >, we will refund your CHF 250 in full, no questions asked. Card payments are refunded via
    Stripe to the original payment method; crypto payments are refunded to the wallet address the
    payment was sent from.
  </p>

  <h2>Signing secrets</h2>
  <p>
    You upload your own certificates and keystores; we store and use them only to sign your builds.
    We cannot recover a lost Android keystore — see our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Service availability</h2>
  <p>
    MobileFlow is under active development. We aim for high availability but do not guarantee
    uninterrupted service, and build times outside our control — such as GitHub Actions queue times
    — are not covered by any SLA.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Don't use MobileFlow to build or distribute unlawful, infringing, or malicious software, or to
    attempt to abuse or disrupt the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the product evolves. Material changes will be communicated before
    they take effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
